meta {
	name: ConcurrentRequestCreation
	seq: 12
}

auth {
	mode: inherit
}

docs {
	# Creating the same request several times at once (#3931)

	When the frontend calls the create endpoint several times in quick succession, the calls can
	all read that no request exists yet and all create one. The result is several pending
	requests for the same package or resource, and the approver is asked more than once.
	These scenarios send identical or conflicting create calls at the same time and check that
	the API ends with one pending request, never answers 500, and gives each caller the same
	request.

	Each subfolder is one scenario. The files inside are the scenario steps, named
	`NN_GIVEN|WHEN|THEN|AND|CLEANUP_...` and ordered by `seq`. A scenario starts from a known
	state, rejects what it created, and can run standalone or repeatedly.

	## What these scenarios cannot check

	The bug also queues duplicate notifications in the outbox. No API exposes the outbox, so the
	scenarios only check the requests. And since the calls travel over the network, the race is
	not certain to happen on every run: a failing run proves the bug, a passing run does not
	prove it is gone.

	## Environments and the fix

	The Azure DevOps post-deployment run executes the whole `test` folder in every environment.
	Every step starts with `skipOutsideEnabledEnvironments()` from `helpers.js`:

	- `enabledEnvironments`: where AccessManagement.Enduser.RequestV2Api is on and the seed data
		is verified.
	- `fixedEnvironments`: where the fix for #3931 is deployed. Scenarios 01, 02 and 03 expect the
		fixed behaviour and are skipped everywhere else. Add an environment when the fix reaches it.
		Scenario 04 checks what already works today and runs in every enabled environment.

	## Tokens and fixtures

	Personas live in `testdata/delegationrequest-scenarios/<tokenEnv>.js` under
	`concurrentRequestCreation`, from the `be-om-tilgang` fixtures. The requester is an
	organisation acting through its innehaver, the approver a private person connected to it.
	The pair and resource are shared with `ResourceRequestRightKeysV2`; the GIVEN steps of both
	suites reject what the other leaves pending.
}
